    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Wk6b9gmd85yK5yANHJbYHA)_\n\n## Summary\nIntegrates the pasted `font-cycle.el` into `sp-fonts` (doc section \"Font cycling\" + tangled module), on top of the existing fontaine presets.\n\n- `M-x sp-font-cycle` opens a transient menu: left/right cycle the installed families, up/down change the size (reusing `font-size-increase`/`-decrease`), `y` copies the `set-face-attribute` form, `r` restores the starting font, `q` quits.\n- The family list is `sp-font-cycle-families` (your list) plus the default families of `fontaine-presets`, filtered by `find-font`.\n- **`s` saves permanently**: it asks for a fontaine preset (current one by default) and rewrites `:default-family` / `:default-height` of that preset in `docs/tangles/ui/sp-fonts.org` *and* `libraries/modules/ui/sp-fonts.el` (so the tangle check stays green), updates the preset table row in the doc, then `y-or-n-p` offers to `load` the module and re-apply the preset. It refuses if a buffer visiting either file is modified.\n- No key is bound (`C-c f` is taken); bind `sp-font-cycle` where you like.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Tangle of `sp-fonts.org` matches the module (Emacs 29.3 batch, `tools/tangle-all.el`).\n- [x] Rewrite function run on temp copies of the org and el: preset edited in both, table row updated, idempotent, unknown preset errors.\n- [ ] In the real Emacs: `M-x sp-font-cycle`, cycle, `s`, answer `y` to the reload; check `git diff`.\n- [ ] Menu look/keys (`<left>`, `<up>`) were not seen on screen (no graphical Emacs here).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAYno2cqRGAJ4GxxdW)_",
